- [ ]  4 | Add Support for Data Tables

Learn how to use data tables with the building tool. This will make the tool more flexible since data tables are used to get all models in the project. Data tables are useful for larger sets of data, like multiple modular meshes of the walls.

- [ ]  5 | Create Base Roof Setup

Learn how to create a base roof geometry on the buildings. Next you will see how you could create a roof. You will start by making a basic roof that would work in multiple situations.

- [ ]  6 | Improve Roofs

Learn how to add more variation and style options to the roof. The tools will take the base roof geometry from the last lesson then enhance it to let the tool choose a different variation. This has the potential to create many variations and styles.

- [ ]  7 | Final Tweaks for Unreal

Learn how to use the final Titan Building tool in Unreal. The tool is almost ready and here you will see a couple settings that need to be changed. This can go from doing some cleanup such as adding snapping or checking if the correct attributes are set on the roofs.

